Description:
	Administration reports section body: a figures strip, then two record lists.

	Both lists are genuine database tables that grow with the platform, so both are counted, paged
	and searched in the database through the shared controls, exactly as every other list in the
	LMS. They previously rendered every course and every company in one unbounded table, which is
	why the active theme was left to bolt a row filter onto them - a filter that searched only the
	rows already on the page and silently disagreed with the total beside it.

	The two datasets keep separate pagination and separate search state, as Enrolments does with
	requests and enrolments, because they grow at different rates and a reader paging one must not
	lose their place in the other.

	WARNING: never write an F3 tag, an angle bracket or a comment delimiter inside a template
	comment. F3 parses its own tags inside comments, and a delimiter written here ends the comment
	early and leaks the remainder onto the page.
